                <pb facs="0139" n="105" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg105"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 66.</note>
                <head>Mr. E. B. Washburne to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 268.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-09-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 26, 1870</date>. (Received September
                    8.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have the honor to send you herewith a copy of the telegraphic dispatch of Mr.
                    Motley in regard to the protest of Count Bismarck, and the reply of the Prince
                    de la Tour d’Auvergne, which carry with them their own explanation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. B. WASHBURNE.</signed></closer>




